      "value": "Hey @{654a7d1f1870ff9faf0911e8|full_name}\n\nResetting the avatar while moving around seems to be a good way to trigger the issue (video attached)\n\nDoing the same but without moving does seem to trigger it though (no video)\n\nI assume there's some discrepancy happening somewhere in the loading if the trackers are not in the same position as when they were saved. \n\nMaybe it could have something to do with the avatar's root position potentially not being the same as the hip's and that not being accounted for (if it's the case).\n\nThe intensity of the problem could also be FPS-dependant. I am currently running my Valve Index at 80hz, but I was running it at 90hz before; never above. The attached video is at a stable 80fps in my home world.\n\nThe offset is pretty much always going to my right as far as I can recall...\n\nI use 3 Vive trackers, 80% tracker motion prediction and lock-all.\n\nAttached video (Canny doesn't accept MP4s): https://files.catbox.moe/sdiylf.mp4\n\nAttached is a picture of a before/after of the video with lines that are about straight (I tried). And yes, my head is hunched to the right, it's always light that...",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
